# Requirements traceability for a floor beam

The requirement diagram ties each requirement to the check that satisfies it. The checks follow,
so a reviewer can go from a requirement to its number.

```mermaid
requirementDiagram
  requirement strength {
    id: R1
    text: Design moment within capacity
    risk: high
    verifymethod: analysis
  }
  requirement serviceability {
    id: R2
    text: Deflection within span over 300
    risk: medium
    verifymethod: analysis
  }
  element bending_check {
    type: sheet check
  }
  element deflection_check {
    type: sheet check
  }
  bending_check - satisfies -> strength
  deflection_check - satisfies -> serviceability
```

## Inputs
L: 6 m | span
w: 10 kN/m | design load
w_s: 6.5 kN/m | service load
E: 200000 MPa | elastic modulus
I: 85000000 mm⁴ | second moment of area
phiMs: 140 kN*m | design capacity of the section

## R1: strength
Mstar: w * L^2 / 8 -> kN*m | design moment
if Mstar <= phiMs: "R1 met." else: "R1 not met."

## R2: serviceability
delta: 5 * w_s * L^4 / (384 * E * I) -> mm | midspan deflection
delta_lim: L / 300 -> mm | limit
if delta <= delta_lim: "R2 met." else: "R2 not met."
